  "notes": "Patch ordering remains lexical. Dependencies describe hard prerequisites. validation_checkpoint=false keeps cumulative source state until a later corrective patch closes the group; 0008/0009 are validated after 0010, and 0011 is validated after 0012. 0013 fixes player annotation lookup for online-only players. 0014 adds verified, exact-version panel patch hot update through the existing job queue; 0015 displays the existing audit response summary in desktop and mobile operation logs; 0016 restores the patch-update OpenAPI contract, and 0017 adds click-through audit response details without expanding stored response data; 0018 persists conservative player presence sessions and totals from the official REST players endpoint without treating an unavailable source as an all-player logout; 0019 resolves stable Releases from the published workspace before falling back to the GitHub REST API, avoiding anonymous shared-IP rate limits and accepting deployment token aliases; 0020 portals the audit response dialog to document.body so the app-main scroll/transform stacking context cannot clip or empty it; 0021 captures bounded, recursively redacted structured write-response details in the existing audit message field; 0022 exposes PalPanel's pinned Rust UID remapper as a managed co-op host migration workflow, enables its pinned Oodle/PlM decoder, derives the dedicated UID from SteamID64, preserves the managed import, stops a running server, publishes the migrated world under Pal/Saved/SaveGames/0, atomically switches GameUserSettings.ini DedicatedServerName, and restarts only when the server was previously running; 0023 aggregates localized non-empty inventory slots across player, base-linked, and unresolved containers, exposing read-only search, owner scope, category, sorting, and location details without changing sav-cli or save data; 0024 uses player-presence history and the current server save index to baseline existing players, then persists frozen item and Pal-template gift plans with serialized batch delivery, retry, and offline-to-online rearm semantics; 0025 resolves the active WorldID from DedicatedServerName, isolates presence plus starter-gift configuration and progress by world, uses per-world workers, and replaces manual starter-item entry with bounded categorized multi-select catalogs. 0026 redesigns the starter-gift workspace; 0027 tracks WorldID-scoped unattended inventory positive deltas; 0028 restores the global inventory Sidebar entry; 0029 keeps starter-item and Pal-template ordering independent of selection so focused rows do not jump to the top of their scroll containers; 0030 adds a read-only player archive summary using existing player, Pal, presence, and coordinate data with broad Chinese region estimates. 0031 reads PalID, nickname, and level from each bounded PalDefender template JSON instead of inferring the Pal from its filename; 0032 reads optional template index JSON files from the PalDefender Templates directory, enriches templates by filename, and exposes index/category filters while preserving template JSON PalID as the identity source. 0034 adds read-only Pal inventory quality/location fields, compound filters, stable sorting, and terminal page-row-column display from existing save-index fields. 0035 normalizes optional Pal instance identifiers before PlayerSummary Map keys and prevents undefined-key TypeScript failures. 0036 exposes a runtime API catalog backed by the actual Gin route table and repository documentation. 0037 removes the invalid PalDefender player Status online gate and resolves currently online official REST players by normalized UserID/PlayerUID across the complete PalDefender account list.",
